00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.213
Part 1.

35
00:02:21.493 --> 00:02:23.029
The System in One Page.

36
00:02:24.279 --> 00:02:25.943
Why food delivery is hard.

37
00:02:26.223 --> 00:02:31.151
Food delivery is a three-sided real-time marketplace with perishable goods:

38
00:02:31.431 --> 00:02:36.786
Customers expect delivery in 30 minutes or less, and they expect the ETA they were promised.

39
00:02:37.066 --> 00:02:42.463
Restaurants cook with variable prep times, which depend on kitchen load, the dish and staff.

40
00:02:42.743 --> 00:02:46.882
Delivery partners (riders) are independent and move around the city.

41
00:02:47.162 --> 00:02:50.106
Their supply varies by hour, weather and incentives.

42
00:02:50.386 --> 00:02:53.821
Food degrades with time: cold food means a bad rating.

43
00:02:54.101 --> 00:02:57.791
Riders shouldn't wait at restaurants, and food shouldn't wait for riders.

44
00:02:59.141 --> 00:03:11.045
Demand is extremely peaky: lunch from 12:30 to 14:00;. dinner from 19:30 to 22:30;. rain spikes it further;. big matches spike it even more.

45
00:03:11.325 --> 00:03:16.723
Every decision trades off customer speed, rider utilisation and restaurant efficiency.

46
