00:04:52.213 --> 00:04:53.557
Here is a quick table:

82
00:04:53.837 --> 00:04:55.160
Quantity, and Value.

83
00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.251
Cities:

84
00:04:56.531 --> 00:04:57.811
500 plus.

85
00:04:58.091 --> 00:04:59.029
Restaurants:

86
00:04:59.309 --> 00:05:01.016
250k active.

87
00:05:01.296 --> 00:05:03.216
Active delivery partners at peak:

88
00:05:03.496 --> 00:05:05.736
300k online at dinner peak.

89
00:05:06.016 --> 00:05:06.805
Orders:

90
00:05:07.085 --> 00:05:14.189
3M per day; peak ~600 orders per second at 20:30 (rain days 1.5 to 2 times ).

91
00:05:14.469 --> 00:05:15.664
Home feed loads:

92
00:05:15.944 --> 00:05:19.144
50M per day; ~3k per second at peak.

93
00:05:19.424 --> 00:05:20.917
Rider location pings:

94
00:05:21.197 --> 00:05:27.277
300k riders times 1 ping or 4 s = 75k pings per second.

95
00:05:27.557 --> 00:05:31.589
Order state events: ~20 per order, then 60M per day.

96
00:05:31.869 --> 00:05:33.192
Dispatch decisions:

97
00:05:33.472 --> 00:05:37.376
Every few seconds per zone, each over hundreds of orders and riders.

98
00:05:38.726 --> 00:05:40.113
Estimation highlights.

99
00:05:40.393 --> 00:05:41.395
Feed cost.

100
00:05:41.675 --> 00:05:53.537
Each feed call must know, for the customer's location: which restaurants are serviceable right now (open, within radius, rider availability);. their ETAs and fees;. personalised ranking.

101
00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:59.004
That is several hundred restaurants evaluated in 300 ms.

102
00:05:59.284 --> 00:06:07.796
Serviceability and ETA must come from precomputed, zone-level signals refreshed every minute or so, not computed fresh per request.

103
00:06:08.076 --> 00:06:08.993
Dispatch.

104
00:06:09.273 --> 00:06:19.577
600 orders per second nationwide spread across ~1,500 zones is ~0.4 orders per second per zone on average.

105
00:06:19.857 --> 00:06:27.111
Hot zones (Koramangala at 20:30) see 5 to 10 orders per second with hundreds of riders nearby.

106
00:06:28.461 --> 00:06:35.373
Batch assignment every 10 to 30 seconds per zone keeps the optimisation problem small (§6.4).

107
00:06:35.653 --> 00:06:37.082
Location ingestion.

108
00:06:37.362 --> 00:06:43.463
75k pings per second goes through a geo-indexed in-memory store for riders near X.

109
00:06:43.743 --> 00:06:47.135
Pings are also streamed to Kafka for tracking and analytics.

110
00:06:48.485 --> 00:06:49.360
Part 2.

111
00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:50.600
Requirements.

112
