00:39:38.254 --> 00:39:39.150
Part 9.

586
00:39:39.430 --> 00:39:41.670
Security, Privacy and Compliance.

587
00:39:42.920 --> 00:39:49.085
Food safety: an FSSAI licence is required for listing restaurants, and displayed (VERIFY).

588
00:39:49.365 --> 00:39:50.112
Tax:

589
00:39:50.392 --> 00:39:58.755
GST on restaurant services through e-commerce operators is collected and paid by the platform (Section 9(5), VERIFY).

590
00:39:59.035 --> 00:40:01.360
TCS or TDS on settlements.

591
00:40:01.640 --> 00:40:02.941
Invoices per order.

592
00:40:03.221 --> 00:40:10.283
Gig workers: the Code on Social Security includes gig and platform workers (VERIFY notification status);.

593
00:40:11.633 --> 00:40:24.539
state laws (for example, Rajasthan's 2023 act, Karnataka's ordinance or act; VERIFY) may require registration, welfare fees and transparency on algorithms and payouts.

594
00:40:24.819 --> 00:40:30.345
Designs should support earnings transparency, grievance redressal and data on working hours.

595
00:40:30.625 --> 00:40:41.014
Consumer protection: transparent fees (no drip pricing), clear cancellation and refund policies, grievance officers, and dark patterns guidelines (VERIFY).

596
00:40:41.294 --> 00:40:42.211
Privacy:

597
00:40:43.561 --> 00:40:52.244
masked phone numbers;. rider locations shown only during active orders;. customer addresses visible to riders only during delivery;.

598
00:40:52.524 --> 00:40:54.380
DPDP Act compliance.

599
00:40:54.660 --> 00:40:55.513
Payments:

600
00:40:55.793 --> 00:40:59.697
PCI-DSS, tokenisation and RBI rules (VERIFY).

601
00:40:59.977 --> 00:41:01.108
Rider safety:

602
00:41:01.388 --> 00:41:06.081
SOS button, insurance, and no penalties that encourage unsafe speeding.

603
00:41:06.361 --> 00:41:13.401
Avoid ETAs that pressure riders unrealistically, a point raised publicly about 10-minute delivery (VERIFY).

604
00:41:14.751 --> 00:41:15.605
Part 10.

605
00:41:15.885 --> 00:41:17.805
Reliability and Operations.

606
00:41:19.055 --> 00:41:33.156
Peak readiness: pre-scale for dinner and events;. load-test order placement;. protect the critical path (place order, restaurant notification, dispatch, tracking);. shed non-critical features (recommendation widgets) first.

607
00:41:33.436 --> 00:41:39.196
Degraded modes: if the ETA model fails, fall back to heuristic ETAs from zone averages;.

608
00:41:40.546 --> 00:41:50.679
if dispatch optimisation is slow, fall back to a greedy nearest-rider assignment;. if the restaurant app is offline, fall back to automated calls (IVR).

609
00:41:50.959 --> 00:42:00.431
City ops centre: dashboards per zone (stress, breach rates, rider supply), manual levers and incident playbooks for rain, festivals and outages.

610
00:42:00.711 --> 00:42:04.423
Observability: order funnel conversion;. acceptance times;.

611
00:42:05.773 --> 00:42:08.824
rider assignment delay;. rider wait at restaurants;.

612
00:42:09.104 --> 00:42:13.925
ETA error by component;. complaint rates;. refund costs;. payment success.

613
00:42:14.205 --> 00:42:22.739
Restaurant reliability: acceptance rate, cancellation rate, prep accuracy and complaint rate are fed back into ranking and onboarding.

614
00:42:24.089 --> 00:42:25.091
